# CTT and strong baseline source audit

Inspected 2026-10-12. Sources are primary papers and author repositories; no performance claim below is a local measurement.

CTT: https://arxiv.org/html/2301.05974v3 (2025-03-28 revision), Algorithm 1, Proposition 1, Remark 3, Appendix C, Section 5 and Appendix H. Equal raw-bin sizes and a common compression construction underpin the exchangeability/rank proof. Randomized ties and, where needed, boundary randomization matter. The paper uses alpha=.05, s=32, delta=.5 and 400 repetitions in its main configuration. The author README provides a smaller native Gaussian d=10, n=16384, mean_diff=.048, B=39, s_permute=16 example. Main Gaussian displacement and the smaller README displacement must not be conflated. Kernel bandwidth and all selection/compression/calibration cost must be charged.

Source pins and byte hashes: sources/native_code_manifest_v1.json. Goodpoints commit 181b12ade5dd02a61b65ed5cb9444c916fa3135f; Cheap Permutations commit 8c775da7dc317cbdb84ed768ce93fda55a9e2f2f. MIT licenses retained. Individual downloaded UTF-8 files were checked against Git blob object hashes after correcting an extra newline introduced by local materialization. These files were not executed as a native benchmark this turn.

Strong successor baseline: Cheap Permutation Testing, https://arxiv.org/pdf/2502.07672, v3 2026-07-21; https://github.com/microsoft/cheap-permutations. Algorithm 1 and Section 6 already cover bin-based permutation acceleration and RFF combinations. Permutation cost O(Bs^2) does not remove initial exact-kernel O(n^2) cost. The source comparison includes exact, block/incomplete and random-feature alternatives, with common compiled kernel routines. Merely streaming RFF bin means or adding early permutation stopping is not a supported novelty claim. The 2026 Nystrom competitor https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.13570 (v4 2026-04-20) remains a required closer protocol/code audit; only its abstract was recovered here.

Concrete source question for next work: goodpoints/ctt.py applies signs +1/-1 then divides signed_matrix_sum by a*b for a,b group-bin counts. goodpoints/cttc.pyx directly evaluates sum_ij K_ij sign_i sign_j. At unequal a,b this is proportional to ||a mu_A-b mu_B||^2/(ab), rather than ||mu_A-mu_B||^2. With identical unit features and a=1,b=3, the former is 4/3 whereas true MMD is zero. Equal counts recover the intended mean difference. This source-derived observation concerns the estimand, not null calibration: a permutation test can remain exact for a different statistic. Published balanced experiments are not refuted. Confirm the complete calling path and native function before any software-defect claim or unequal-sample extension. Source rff/lrctt and Cheap Permutations feature paths also require count-normalization review.

Bandwidth tuning audit remains open: the paper's median heuristic samples 512 points from each group. Whether fitting is fixed, pooled/permutation-invariant, conditioned upon, or recomputed is part of the precise guarantee and must not be handwaved as a defect or automatically valid. Balanced native benchmark first; no claim that an adaptive allocation method is ready.
